  <prompt>Worktree C:\wt097, branch fix/event-complete-and-todo-reassign (off origin/master). Prove, then fix, two suspected broken write paths that the Console's Do lane will rely on.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE engineer. A write path that always fails is a defect to diagnose, never noise (ADR-038 project rule 2).</role>
  <goal>Completing a task event and reassigning a To Do each write values the live Dataverse schema accepts, proven by a real create-read against spaarkedev1, with tests that would have caught the original defects.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Found 2026-10-05 while checking the v4 prototype's actions against the real solution (main session, notes/v4-prototype-vs-solution.md). (1) POST /api/v1/events/{id}/complete (EventEndpoints.cs:92) writes statuscode 5 (EventDto.cs constants: Completed = 5; DataverseWebApiService.cs:530-541), but the live sprk_event statuscode option set reportedly has Completed = 659490002 and no 5. (2) TodoDetail.tsx (~line 645) binds sprk_AssignedTo to /systemusers(...), but the live sprk_todo.sprk_assignedto column reportedly targets contact. Both claims come from code reading only.</background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: own PR against master. Prove each defect against the LIVE schema first (Dataverse MCP describe / read_query, or Web API metadata, read-only), and if possible reproduce the failure (e.g. a create + update + read on a throwaway record in spaarkedev1, deleted afterwards). Report evidence; if a claim is false, say so and change nothing for it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: fix the cause, not the symptom. Find every other place that uses the same wrong constant or binding (grep all of src/ for the status constants, statuscode 5 on sprk_event, and sprk_AssignedTo/systemusers binds) and fix each, or list why not. Prefer the existing shared option-set constants if any exist; do not invent a second source of truth.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests asserting an option-set value or a lookup target must be paired with something touching the real schema (project testing rule 1): add or extend a test that reads the live metadata, or a schema-parity test against the checked-in data-model doc that itself was verified live today.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: CLAUDE.md section 10 applies to BFF changes (placement statement, publish size vs a fresh master build from short paths, vulnerable-package check). Never use --no-verify or bare git stash. You cannot write .claude/.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8.</step>
    <step order="1">Read both code paths and the live metadata; prove or disprove each defect.</step>
    <step order="2">Fix every occurrence; add tests that would have caught them.</step>
    <step order="3">Real create-read (and update) against spaarkedev1 for each fixed path; clean up test records.</step>
    <step order="4">Build, targeted tests, full BFF suite once (report contention honestly), publish size, open the PR, report back.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Each defect is proven or disproven against the live schema, with evidence in the PR body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every occurrence of a proven defect is fixed, or listed with a reason.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A real write against spaarkedev1 succeeds for each fixed path and is read back with the expected value.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test fails on the old code and passes on the new.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A PR against master is open with the evidence in its body.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Created 2026-10-05 by the main session. Owner rule: fix found defects now, in their own PR when unrelated to ontology.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
